<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-09T05:08:52+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Mon, 09 Nov 2026 05:08:52 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Baby pufferfish inherit a nearly non-toxic chemical from their mothers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135640976.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a fascinating discovery, researchers have found that mother pufferfish provide their larvae with a nearly non-toxic chemical that effectively helps them escape predators. This chemical deters potential threats by making them unpalatable, thus improving the young fish's chances of survival. Additionally, this same chemical intriguingly attracts other pufferfish, revealing a unique dual role that aids in their survival strategies during vulnerable stages.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/shocking-discovery-baby-pufferfish-use-chemical-defense-from-mothers-to-avoid-predators/articleshow/135640976.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/shocking-discovery-baby-pufferfish-use-chemical-defense-from-mothers-to-avoid-predators/articleshow/135640976.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T04:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135641144,imgsize-1194593.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Stanford scientists have built a fingernail-sized chip that turns jumbled light into clean beams]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135641393.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Stanford University researchers have developed a groundbreaking chip that effectively segregates mixed light into its individual components. This novel technology facilitates the analysis of coherence modes of light that were once challenging to identify. Utilizing advanced photonic techniques, the chip can enhance applications in fields like imaging and astronomy, potentially transforming our understanding of microscopic particles and faraway celestial phenomena.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/stanford-scientists-create-revolutionary-fingernail-sized-chip-to-separate-mixed-light-boosting-microscopy-astronomy-and-photography/articleshow/135641393.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/stanford-scientists-create-revolutionary-fingernail-sized-chip-to-separate-mixed-light-boosting-microscopy-astronomy-and-photography/articleshow/135641393.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T04:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135641543,imgsize-1155511.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet 14-year-old Jacob who grows 7,000 tomato plants for his business]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135606415.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/meet-jacob-the-14-year-old-from-england-who-started-selling-tomato-plants-from-a-small-cart-and-now-grows-7000-plants-with-customers-ordering-from-overseas/articleshow/135606415.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/meet-jacob-the-14-year-old-from-england-who-started-selling-tomato-plants-from-a-small-cart-and-now-grows-7000-plants-with-customers-ordering-from-overseas/articleshow/135606415.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T04:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135606596,imgsize-154859.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[16-year-old builds free wildfire warning checker, teaches California seniors to use it after brush fire]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135616807.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Vedant Thakker created the Red Flag Check application to evaluate wildfire risks utilizing data from the National Weather Service. This innovative tool classifies residential locations under red flag warnings into four specific risk categories, empowering local residents. It is specially designed for older adults who may face increased vulnerability during wildfires.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-vedant-thakker-the-16-year-old-california-student-who-built-a-free-wildfire-warning-checker-showing-four-location-categories-and-is-teaching-fremont-seniors-how-to-use-it-after-a-nearby-brush-fire/articleshow/135616807.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-vedant-thakker-the-16-year-old-california-student-who-built-a-free-wildfire-warning-checker-showing-four-location-categories-and-is-teaching-fremont-seniors-how-to-use-it-after-a-nearby-brush-fire/articleshow/135616807.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T03:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135617233,imgsize-80763.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Firehouse Townhouse Sells: Former Manhattan station fetches $19m; includes underground jazz club]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135615117.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A historic fire station in Manhattan has been transformed into a luxury townhouse and sold for $19 million. It originally served the community as a firehouse for over a century before being decommissioned. The property underwent extensive renovations, highlighting its unique features such as an underground jazz club. Notably, the townhouse retains elements of its industrial past while incorporating modern living spaces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/built-in-1864-as-a-manhattan-fire-station-this-7281-square-foot-property-became-a-five-level-townhouse-with-its-own-underground-jazz-club-it-has-now-sold-for-19-million-in-new-york/articleshow/135615117.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/built-in-1864-as-a-manhattan-fire-station-this-7281-square-foot-property-became-a-five-level-townhouse-with-its-own-underground-jazz-club-it-has-now-sold-for-19-million-in-new-york/articleshow/135615117.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T03:54:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135615320,imgsize-1842586.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Historic Brooklyn mansion returns to market for $20.99M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135630147.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Once a forgotten gem, a historic mansion in Brooklyn Heights from 1852 has been meticulously transformed and is now available for $14.99 million. The adjacent carriage house can be purchased separately for $6 million. After a decade-long renovation focused on preserving its original beauty while integrating luxury amenities, this estate invites potential buyers to explore various living arrangements, from family homes to vibrant workspaces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2010-a-developer-paid-1-25-million-for-two-wrecked-brooklyn-properties-sixteen-years-later-the-1852-mansion-is-listed-for-20-99-million-following-a-long-rebuild-alongside-its-renovated-carriage-house/articleshow/135630147.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2010-a-developer-paid-1-25-million-for-two-wrecked-brooklyn-properties-sixteen-years-later-the-1852-mansion-is-listed-for-20-99-million-following-a-long-rebuild-alongside-its-renovated-carriage-house/articleshow/135630147.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T03:48:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135630409,imgsize-172268.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[High Court dismisses farm claims by Richard Scott’s son and stepmother]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135604917.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindi