6.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Billionaire couple's $50 million gift leads to new UC Davis research centre]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135606232.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/billionaire-couple-lynda-and-stewart-resnick-pledged-50-million-to-uc-davis-in-2022-their-34000-square-foot-agricultural-research-centre-opened-in-may-2026/articleshow/135606232.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/billionaire-couple-lynda-and-stewart-resnick-pledged-50-million-to-uc-davis-in-2022-their-34000-square-foot-agricultural-research-centre-opened-in-may-2026/articleshow/135606232.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T03:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135606387,imgsize-1818952.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How two Wisconsin students built a volunteer network to fight hunger]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135605390.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Middleton, Wisconsin, Noah Duckett and Wyatt Ehrhardt launched a food drive aimed at tackling food insecurity. This initiative blossomed into Meals Matter, a national non-profit featuring over 35 student-led chapters. With more than $550,000 raised and countless young volunteers participating nationwide, both founders were honored with The Diana Award, showcasing how youth can lead transformative social change.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-two-wisconsin-teens-launched-a-food-drive-at-their-high-school-by-2026-meals-matter-had-expanded-to-over-35-chapters-and-3500-volunteers-collecting-more-than-550000-in-cash-and-food-donations/articleshow/135605390.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-two-wisconsin-teens-launched-a-food-drive-at-their-high-school-by-2026-meals-matter-had-expanded-to-over-35-chapters-and-3500-volunteers-collecting-more-than-550000-in-cash-and-food-donations/articleshow/135605390.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T01:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135605686,imgsize-330893.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rotten Roots: family turns yard into walk-through Halloween haunt; visitors trigger effects]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135578353.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Pennsylvania, a family has dedicated five years to crafting an enchanting Halloween experience known as Rotten Roots. This immersive yard display combines a thrilling storyline of witches and alien invaders with interactive decorations, enhanced through a special app. As they continue to expand their attraction with new characters and mechanics, the family fosters deeper bonds within the local Halloween enthusiast community.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/what-began-as-a-small-halloween-graveyard-five-years-ago-has-become-a-pennsylvania-familys-walk-through-yard-attraction-with-towering-animatronics-alien-spider-battles-a-corn-path-and-a-custom-fog-system/articleshow/135578353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/what-began-as-a-small-halloween-graveyard-five-years-ago-has-become-a-pennsylvania-familys-walk-through-yard-attraction-with-towering-animatronics-alien-spider-battles-a-corn-path-and-a-custom-fog-system/articleshow/135578353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="ht