ate>2026-11-09T02:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135603752,imgsize-382200.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[2,800-year-old Siberian tomb reveals 1,000 cannabis seeds and evidence of ritual intoxication]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135603594.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A groundbreaking archaeological find at Tunnug 1 in southern Siberia unveiled cannabis seeds within a prince's tomb, dating back 2,800 years. This tomb is tied to intricate funerary rites, including horse sacrifices. Notably, preserved human hair revealed traces of cannabis, hinting at its psychoactive use, which underscores cannabis's significant role in ancient burial customs. Researchers plan to conduct further DNA analysis to deepen the understanding of its historical relevance.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/in-a-2800-year-old-siberian-tomb-researchers-found-about-1000-cannabis-seeds-and-chemical-traces-in-human-hair-suggesting-ritual-intoxication-among-people-buried-alongside-sacrificed-horses-and-other-remains/articleshow/135603594.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/in-a-2800-year-old-siberian-tomb-researchers-found-about-1000-cannabis-seeds-and-chemical-traces-in-human-hair-suggesting-ritual-intoxication-among-people-buried-alongside-sacrificed-horses-and-other-remains/articleshow/135603594.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T00:54:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135603775,imgsize-110897.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Mexico artist gives a 1953 Chevy Bel Air a second life as a jackrabbit]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135601895.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Robert Wilson crafted an impressive sculpture of a jackrabbit from salvaged components of a 1953 Chevrolet Bel Air. Titled Run, this artwork symbolizes the rich heritage of Route 66 through its creative design. Towering at over 10 feet, it is richly detailed to reflect its automotive origins. Situated in Babe Ruth Park, Gallup, this piece celebrates the 100th anniversary of the legendary highway, inviting visitors to appreciate its artistry.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-mexico-artist-spent-more-than-a-year-turning-parts-from-a-1953-chevy-bel-air-into-a-10-foot-tall-1200-pound-jackrabbit-sculpture-celebrating-route-66/articleshow/135601895.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-mexico-artist-spent-more-than-a-year-turning-parts-from-a-1953-chevy-bel-air-into-a-10-foot-tall-1200-pound-jackrabbit-sculpture-celebrating-route-66/articleshow/135601895.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T00:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135602091,imgsize-386029.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[444-million-year-old fossil preserves muscles but loses head and legs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135608285.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/scientists-studied-a-444-million-year-old-marine-fossil-that-preserved-its-muscles-tendons-and-guts-but-lost-its-head-legs-and-outer-shell-they-named-it-after-the-discoverers-mother/articleshow/135608285.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/scientists-studied-a-444-million-year-old-marine-fossil-that-preserved-its-muscles-tendons-and-guts-but-lost-its-head-legs-and-outer-shell-they-named-it-after-the-discoverers-mother/articleshow/135608285.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T00:47:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135608594,imgsize-179200.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Georgia couple's $40,000 basement renovation sparks divorce property dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135603507.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-georgia-couple-spent-40000-turning-the-husbands-pre-marital-home-basement-into-a-separate-space-for-her-parents-after-divorce-an-appeals-court-ordered-the-property-split-to-be-reconsidered/articleshow/135603507.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-georgia-couple-spent-40000-turning-the-husbands-pre-marital-home-basement-into-a-separate-space-for-her-parents-after-divorce-an-appeals-court-ordered-the-property-split-to-be-reconsidered/articleshow/135603507.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T00:49:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135603988,imgsize-121043.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Omaha apartment owner's civil rights lawsuit over 2018 closure rejected by appeals court]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135663645.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A federal appeals court confirmed the dismissal of civil rights claims by AB Realty against Omaha officials. The lawsuit arose after the city shut down a building due to code violations in 2018. Despite the claims alleging Fourth, Fifth, and Fourteenth Amendment violations, the court found insufficient evidence to support them. The ruling highlighted that the city had acted according to legal standards during the inspections.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-an-omaha-apartment-complex-closed-amid-code-complaints-forcing-tenants-to-move-after-reopening-in-2021-its-owner-pursued-a-lawsuit-against-the-city-but-a-2026-appeals-ruling-rejected-the-claims/articleshow/135663645.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-an-omaha-apartment-complex-closed-amid-code-complaints-forcing-tenants-to-move-after-reopening-in-2021-its-owner-pursued-a-lawsuit-against-the-city-but-a-2026-appeals-ruling-rejected-the-claims/articleshow/135663645.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-09T00:12:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135664735,imgsize-108104.cms"/></item></channel></rss>